# BrandVault Core Standards

Follow `BrandVault-Project-Plan (1).md` for architecture, routes, and API envelopes.

## Size & cleanliness

- Keep every new/edited file **under 150 lines**. Split when approaching the limit.
- No dead code, commented-out blocks, or drive-by refactors outside the task.
- Prefer small, single-purpose functions and classes.

## Naming

- Use meaningful names: `$assetRepository`, `folderDepth`, `primaryColor` — never `x`, `c`, `t`, `data2`, `tmp`.
- Booleans read as questions/states: `$isFolderEmpty`, `$hasChildren`.
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for true constants; enums for fixed domain sets.

## Architecture (non-negotiable)

- **Modular** layout under `app/Modules/{Module}/` (Controllers, Requests, Services, Repositories, Models, Policies, routes).
- **Service / Repository** pattern: controllers orchestrate only; services own business rules; repositories own Eloquent queries.
- Cross-user isolation: every query/policy scopes by `user_id`.

## Commits

- Imperative, focused subject (≈72 chars). Body explains *why* when needed.
- One logical change per commit; do not mix formatting with features.
